@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;isolation] native-vm-watch-read-only
The helper MUST only open a pidfd for the given PID, read the unit cgroup's
cgroup.procs and cgroup.events, and watch them. It MUST NOT signal processes,
write any cgroup or file, change namespace, or read guest data. No setuid or
capabilities; stdout carries only the fixed lines armed, exited and error.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] vm-watch-hegel-and-native
Hegel properties MUST cover the PID and cgroup argument grammar, the
`parse_cli` lattice (a target exactly when both selectors accept two UTF-8
arguments) and the cgroup.events/procs parsers against independent models.
Kernel exit timing is evidenced by the in-build child test where cgroup2 is
readable and by the NixOS vm-watch machine test.
